WEBVTT

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.780
Crap.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.030
What's with this guy?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.030
Yogi.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.710
Kagiri-san!

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.090
Oh, no...

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.650
Yukkin!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.900
Nai-kun, what's the matter?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.950
Yogi. Yogi.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.080
Nai-kun!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.910
Yogi. Yogi. Yogi. Yogi. Yogi. Yogi. Yogi.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.960
Don't tell me they were both killed by those Varuga.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.920
Nai-kun, hide here, and please promise me not to move an inch.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.090
I'll be back soon.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.350
Tsukumo-chan!
Blue Rose
Score 9

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:47.930
Blue Rose
Score 9

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.900
If I tell Uro-san we were defeated by Circus, he's definitely gonna kill us.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.870
Say, aren't you the girl who escaped earlier?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.830
<i>Varuga.</i>

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.540
What happened to my comrades?

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.500
So that's how you look underneath that hood.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.080
Wow...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.840
Amazingly cute!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.300
Answer me!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.960
How should I know?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.090
That blond guy completely lost it all of a sudden.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.680
The black-haired brat must be dead by now!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.470
<i>It can't be true.</i>

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:31.350
<i>But from the way Nai-kun reacted, something must've happened.</i>

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.730
You let down your guard.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.240
This is it!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:55.000
<i>Nai-kun... Yogi...</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.380
Yahoo!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.930
Tsukumo-chan.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.980
Tsukumo-chan!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.820
Karoku-sama...

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.820
Is something wrong?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.320
Karoku-sama...

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.160
Are you all right?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:33.960
Uro, I have a headache, so I want to rest a little bit.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.920
We still have some time until the party.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.930
Please take your time and rest.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.940
Tsukumo-chan, huh?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:12.330
I hear you. Scream more, Nai.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.780
I wonder why I protected you.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.320
<i>He doesn't recognize me.</i>

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.240
<i>What's happening to him?</i>

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.000
Yogi.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.670
What? You want to play?

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.920
Want to play, my ass!

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.340
Ow...

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.090
That's so mean, Ga...Ga...

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:12.470
Ga... What... Gare.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.850
Oh no, Gareki-kun!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.940
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.360
Have I been unconscious?

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.650
I'm so sorry.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:34.370
Thank goodness you're still warm...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.760
Nai?

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.340
Gareki.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.300
Tsukumo-chan...

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.600
Tsukumo-chan was…

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.610
I'm sorry for waking you from your sleep.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.900
Time has no meaning to the people of Research Tower.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.490
Ah... Right.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.870
Let Nai and Gareki wait there after their medical examination.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.240
Um, is there anything I can do?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.580
You belong to the Life Division, so this is not in your expertise.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:23.000
But if it has to do with Varuga, I want to…

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:28.340
Azana, I understand that you feel you can't stand by and do nothing.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.340
Since your family was killed by Varuga, you feel as if it's happening to you.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.560
After you finish your report, get some rest.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.600
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.280
I can't find Uro-san.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.250
Help me look for him too, Kagiri-san!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.500
Should I just shout for him, with all my momentum?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:50.000
We came here without telling him, stupid Kiharu.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.550
We'll get scolded if we attract any attention.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.760
You're giving me hard time.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.260
You're so mean, Uro.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:02.850
Being in that crowd made Karoku-sama feel sick. He told me that he wanted to be alone.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.770
I don't like it. It's so boring!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.610
Where are you going, Erisyuka-sama?

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.560
The bathroom.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.940
Don't follow me!

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.280
<i>I'll look for him in secret.</i>

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.150
<i>Maybe Karoku is at the rooftop.</i>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.450
Gathering of people with masks...

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.910
What's going on?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.290
There's no connection here.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.000
The radio signal is being blocked.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.800
Should I just go ahead and check things out?

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.550
No.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.800
I must get out of here right away.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.450
Oh no, why are you injured like that?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.330
<i>Erisyuka...</i>

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.960
I think I've met you somewhere before...

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.090
Erisyuka-sama!

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.590
There was someone…

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:20.340
Find her!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.180
Yes sir!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.020
Uro!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.640
What happened?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:34.070
The girl from Circus that I met at the train was here... and she was bleeding!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.570
What? That girl escaped?!
What? That girl escaped?!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.490
Who are these people?

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.950
Please forget that you ever saw them.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:51.000
They have absolutely no part in your brilliant life.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.130
Escort her to the room.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:54.920
Yes, sir.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.340
Well, uh...

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.550
Uro-san?

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.600
Why are you here?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.850
What have you done?

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.770
Oh... Well...

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.940
I-It's a rather long story.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.650
Why are you guys so stupid?

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:23.280
Do you have a death wish?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.040
Find that Circus girl.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.540
Half dead is fine!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.380
Bring her to me.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:40.670
There's nothing wrong with either of you.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.760
But as a precaution, you'll be staying here tonight.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.600
Did you find Tsukumo-chan?

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.940
I told you the Second Ship is going all out to find her, didn't I?

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:51.860
Is Yogi…

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.980
What are the results of the examination?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.230
Both of them have no problems in terms of the numerical data.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.570
Ikami, thanks for a job well done.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.990
Nai, Gareki, come with me.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.240
Here's some tea.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.040
Excuse me...

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.910
Take some liquids.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:11.580
How's Yogi?

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.460
I'm about to talk about that.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.290
I have a few questions for you.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.590
Questions?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:20.090
Have you finished his examination?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.880
We've given him appropriate medical procedure.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.130
So he's sleeping now.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.520
Tell me in detail about what happened before and after Yogi's transformation.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.810
Anything will do.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:36.150
When I saw Yogi again, he didn't have that white thing on his face.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.440
Do you mean the patch?

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.320
I also noticed it wasn't there when we returned.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.200
But if he transforms just for losing his patch,

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.450
won't the same thing happen again once he gets it replaced?

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.320
Eh?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:52.160
You weren't there when it happened, but he changed big time,

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.960
even the color of his hair.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.210
It was almost like…

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.130
Gareki.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.930
When was the patch removed?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.470
Huh? So you think?

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.470
Yes, it's related to that.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.520
But as you said,

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.850
I don't make faulty things that cease
to work the instant they come off.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.940
Is he mentally sick?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.110
It's nothing like that.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.950
It occasionally afflicts people
who take on the special duties of Circus.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:26.860
It's an allergy.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.870
<i>He's hiding a lot of details behind his words.</i>

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.040
Give me a proper explanation.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.000
I was caught up in that, you know.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.130
I think I have a right to know.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:46.180
Good grief. I'm the one asking questions.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:51.140
Yogi's sudden transformation in this incident is something irregular.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.890
I received a report stating that there was a interaction with Varuga.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:58.020
Other than that, was there anything else different in Yogi?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:04.990
He was scared and cried in the room full of dolls.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:11.410
Dolls? Was that at the mansion which you investigated?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:15.290
No, to be precise, it was
a hidden room beneath the mansion.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:19.790
Speaking of which, what were the contents of the box Yogi brought back?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.790
What? Box?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.170
Wasn't it in his overcoat?

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.550
The rusty box that was making clattering noises.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.130
No, he didn't have it.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.550
But tell me the details.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.390
Uro-san, well, this is...

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.810
Ki-Kiharu picked it up during the battle.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:45.190
I got caught up in my momentum and thought it was Kagiri-san's toy.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:15:00.120
<i>If Circus had gotten hold of this, it would have been used as evidence against us.</i>

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.590
<i>It could've given a breakthrough to the government.</i>

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:10.010
<i>Circus, toys of the cowardly government.</i>

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.970
<i>They've captured people who were drawn to us,</i>

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:19.270
<i>but those people know nothing, just like lizard tails.</i>

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.190
<i>We can easily replace them.</i>

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.310
It's about Erisyuka-sama.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.940
Tell me about it later.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:32.950
<i>But for the tails, we, the body, are something they long for forever.</i>

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.540
<i>That's why they will never stop cooperating with us.</i>

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:49.720
<i>Because things we're selling them are the love and hope they've been seeking.</i>

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.300
<i>Bestial Varuga...</i>

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.640
<i>Even if I fight recklessly and kill these creatures in front of me,</i>

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.810
<i>there's a greater chance that new enemies will appear.</i>

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.690
<i>I'm all alone right now.</i>

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.110
<i>I should only think about getting back alive.</i>

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:08.820
<i>But...</i>

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.610
<i>If I fail to escape...</i>

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.530
<i>I'll kill myself with my own hands before being captured.</i>

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:25.540
<i>I have to make sure I don't leave anything behind. I won't let them use my body for themselves.</i>

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.720
<i>I should've talked with everyone more.</i>

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.720
<i>I should've stayed together with them more.</i>

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.350
That's because I trust you.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.650
I'm counting on you, Tsukumo.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:47.400
Hirato...

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.650
How could I have such negative thoughts?

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.280
He believed in me. He relied on me.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.040
I'm not going to end my life.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.290
I am a member of Circus!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.920
I'll only die for my friends!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:09.960
At this point, it's just a presumption,

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:16.550
but that box probably contained parts of the Varuga body or something with similar components.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.850
It has been left around for a long time,

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.230
so the components spilled out and possibly filled the air.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:28.770
If that idiot had forgotten to replace the patch,

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:33.570
the effects of containing his allergic reaction would probably be reduced to near zero.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.570
Even then, the chances of him going berserk is less than 50 percent.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.570
Then why?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:45.960
It's a different story if he had inhaled the air containing Varuga components.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:53.210
Having Varuga components inside of his body... would greatly increase the allergic substances within him.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.720
<i>He's hiding something again.</i>

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.800
When the patch came off,

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:01.810
the balance between the allergic substances and his own cells broke down,

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.720
causing him to go berserk.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.520
His condition sounds pretty unstable.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.160
Say, I've been wanting to ask this,

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.750
but what's the mechanism behind Circus members flying and drawing weapons out of nowhere?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:33.500
You should ask that to Hirato–well no, Tsukitachi.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.010
Both Yogi and Tsukumo are currently incapactitated,

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:41.510
so apparently for the time being, you two will be sent to the First Ship.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.010
Lack of sleep will weaken your body.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.180
Go to sleep now.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.320
Nai.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:54.780
Huh?

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:59.610
You totally didn't understand the conversation earlier, did you?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:01.990
I sort of understood it.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.080
Liar.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.630
<i>I really do, Gareki.</i>

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.260
<i>Compared to back then, somehow I understand things more now.</i>

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:24.140
<i>I can tell when you're thinking of Yotaka-san and others.</i>

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:31.600
<i>When you're sleeping in the room, I can sense things falling from above you.</i>

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:38.570
<i>Feelings of sadness, pain, and suffering...</i>

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:44.570
<i>I've never tried asking you because you're
always your usual self when you're awake.</i>

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:53.830
<i>You know, it's always quiet at night, so I'm able to hear even the smallest of voices.</i>

00:19:54.670 --> 00:20:00.840
<i>So If I sleep by the window, I may hear Tsukumo-chan's voice.</i>

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:07.850
<i>I wonder if everyone gets involved in
dangerous things because I'm with them.</i>

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.810
<i>Is that so, Karoku?</i>

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.020
This isn't good, Kagiri-san!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.780
If we don't find that girl, we will seriously be killed.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.950
We definitely must find her.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:56.860
Please don't let out your voice.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.820
If you do, I will break your neck.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.610
Please, put your hands up to your head.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.370
<i>What... a hidden needle.</i>

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.640
I'm sorry, Tsukumo-chan.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.270
Thank you for being kind to Nai.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:52.240
Nai, it's okay to burst into tears of joy, okay?

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.010
Erisyuka-sama wants to see you, Karoku-sama.

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.680
Me too.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.970
Very well. I will tell her so.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:36.430
Nai, where are you now?

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:37.680
Karoku-sama?

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:38.640
Nai.
